# Hello world

*I guess every blog needs one of these*

I've always wanted a blog/website to call my own, and with the rise of
social media, AI slop and enshittification, I decided to take matters into my
own hands, and try to bring back some of the charm of the 90s and early 2000s era
internet back to life.

this isn't my first rodeo trying to make a website/blog. when I was 11 years old I had a blogspot site, one of those "download X software here" blogs that just listed some of my personal list of software I used. The thing is still up to this day with some posts, and seeing that 16 years later put a smile to my face. Such is the power of nostalgia. Back then I had no idea how to make these things, so my aunt's boyfriend helped me with that. 8 years later he became my boss long story shot: him and him and the other guys at the office convinced me to enroll in computer science, but I digress.

every website nowadays looks and feels exactly the same. minimalist, landing-page looking, and with the rise of AI every LLM spits out pretty much the same website layout you've seen hundreds or thousands of times. I miss the 2000's, when every website still had character, and felt like a different world I'd jump into to learn things or just have fun or whatever.

what did I use to build this?
astro

why?
because it's simple, and I like simple.

this is actually the 3rd iteration of this website. I initially made this thing in pure html and css, and like this one, with the least amount of js as possible. but that got annoying after a while, and I decided it was time to migrate to a static site solution.
I don't want to touch wordpress with a 10ft pole, so astro was a logical choice.
astro is great, by the way. you should give it a try.
anyway, this site is lightweight, fast, simple and I think it looks pretty good.

if you've read my about page, you may be wondering why I'm writing this blog in english if I'm brazilian?
english, for better or for worse became the universal language used on planet earth,
so I'm killing two birds with one stone. I reach a wider audience and get to practice my second language more often.

## what am I going to be writing about?

the plan is to document my self *re-discovery* journey in programming amidst
this shit show that is the current state of the web and job and tech market due
to AI slop in code and our daily lives, so I'll going over my personal projects,
tech rants, discoveries, books I'm reading about tech, or pretty much anything else I might have an interest in.

this site will be about my self re-discovery journey in software engineering amidst this shit show that is the current state of the web and the fight against AI slop in code and our daily lives.
I'm sick of being just another web dev withering away while working yet another e-commerce site, so I want to broaden my skills on different areas.

you can expect posts here about my personal projects, discoveries, tech rants, books, music, cars, video games, or whatever my brain decides to hyperfixate on in the future.

